      "one_line": "Serican — wary imperial bureaucracy of the grassland; law, glory.",
      "one_paragraph": "The Serican (Roman + Chinese) are a expansionist imperial bureaucracy people seeded in grassland, plains, hills. They prize law, glory, knowledge, lean toward the military sphere, and field heavy_infantry, crossbowmen, heavy_cavalry. Outsiders are met as wary; their patrons touch law, war, trade."
